      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>PART I, LINE 1A</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION ADOPTED AN EXPENSE REIMBURSEMENT POLICY THAT PERMITS EMPLOYEES TO EXPENSE CERTAIN BUSINESS AND PERSONAL GOODS AND SERVICES, PROVIDED THAT THE GOODS AND SERVICES WILL INCREASE WORK PRODUCTIVITY. PURSUANT TO AN ACCOUNTABLE PLAN, EMPLOYEES MUST SUBMIT ALL EXPENSES WITH A DESCRIPTION OF THE BUSINESS PURPOSE, AND THE ORGANIZATION REVIEWS AND APPROVES ALL EXPENSES FOR REASONABLENESS PRIOR TO APPROVING REIMBURSEMENT. ALL REIMBURSABLE EXPENSES THAT ARE NOT DEDUCTIBLE BUSINESS EXPENSES ARE TREATED AS WAGES TO THE EMPLOYEES. FOUR HIGHEST-COMPENSATED EMPLOYEES LISTED IN SCHEDULE J PART II RECEIVED SUCH PAYMENTS DURING 2024.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>PART I, LINE 7</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION ADOPTED AN EXPENSE REIMBURSEMENT POLICY THAT PERMITS EMPLOYEES TO EXPENSE CERTAIN BUSINESS AND PERSONAL GOODS AND SERVICES, PROVIDED THAT THE GOODS AND SERVICES WILL INCREASE WORK PRODUCTIVITY. PURSUANT TO AN ACCOUNTABLE PLAN, EMPLOYEES MUST SUBMIT ALL EXPENSES WITH A DESCRIPTION OF THE BUSINESS PURPOSE, AND THE ORGANIZATION REVIEWS AND APPROVES ALL EXPENSES FOR REASONABLENESS PRIOR TO APPROVING REIMBURSEMENT. ALL REIMBURSABLE EXPENSES THAT ARE NOT DEDUCTIBLE BUSINESS EXPENSES ARE TREATED AS WAGES TO THE EMPLOYEES.</ExplanationTxt>
